or all 228 questions and independent source-only second reads for all 172 high-risk questions; deterministically compares both sides; and independently source-resolves all 214 disagreements plus the one preserved maker normalization rejection.\n\nThe final artifact-only staging result conserves every question:\n\n`228 = 215 resolver_verified + 13 verified_agreement + 0 safe_rejection + 0 conflict + 0 unresolved`\n\nNo semantic, KG, canonical, production, public, or downstream layer is written.\n\n## Root-cause and custody handling\n\nThe frozen official mark scheme for one terminal question has no printed terminal label despite a complete ordered prefix. The implementation handles that as a generic fail-closed source-absence condition, binds the complete official mark-scheme page chain, and contains no paper-, year-, or question-specific acceptance condition.\n\nChecker producer dialects are admitted only through bounded authenticated adapters. Paper-nested, flat, and canonical nested layouts cannot be mixed; per-question packet inventory hashes remain bound to exact frozen packets; producer terminal inventory hashes are independently reconstructed from frozen v5 bundles; and schema-protocol projections require exact terminal or append-only attestation custody.\n\nThe single maker-normalization rejection preserves both successful provider responses and the safe-rejection history. Its source-only resolver output was corrected before import through append-only supersession so the active decision truthfully uses the checker base while the superseded bytes remain preserved externally.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `PYTHONPATH=. uv run --no-project --python 3.12 --with pymupdf==1.27.2 --with pillow==11.3.0 --with jsonschema python scripts/vlm/__tests__/issue_1686_pre_provider.test.py` — 4/4 PASS\n- `PYTHONPATH=. uv run --no-project --python 3.12 --with pymupdf==1.27.2 --with pillow==11.3.0 --with jsonschema python scripts/vlm/__tests__/issue_1686_final_resolution.test.py` — 8/